{"videoId":"uXvT7hHJfIE","title":"The Perfect Linux Beginners Guide","author":"diinki","authorId":"UCrk2bNxxxLP-Qd77KxBJ3Xg","published":1775669679000,"description":"My linux guide trilogy is now complete!! =w=\nYou can upgrade your very own setup with FlexiSpot! With my code &quot;DIINKI&quot; for an extra $30 discount on the E7 or E7 Pro standing desks, which I highly recommend. Link to the FlexiSpot E7 Pro: https://bit.ly/4t1PmdC\n\n== Good resources &amp; Links: ==\nManual Partitioning on Zorin:\nhttps://help.zorin.com/docs/getting-started/manually-partition-the-drive-to-install-zorin-os/\nZorinOS:\nhttps://zorin.com/\nLink to my Terminal Glossary/Cheat sheet (great as a wallpaper!):\nhttps://github.com/diinki/wallpapers/blob/main/april2026/terminal_glossary_4k_paw.png\nMany colors available as well :)\n\nOur discord server, its strictly SFW, but also restricted to people above 18: https://discord.gg/gleep\n\nChapters:\n0:00 Intro\n1:00 Part 1 - Computer Terminology\n3:21 Part 2 - Choosing the Distro\n6:06 Part 3 - Installing Linux\n10:24 Part 4 - Storage, Accounts, and Zorin\n17:31 Part 5 - The Terminal\n23:59 Part 6 - Package Managers\n28:07 Intermission\n29:22 Part 7 - Conclusion and Final words\n\nAfter making a video where I tried to convince people to swap to linux, its only correct for me to make a beginners guide to linux as well! I wanted this guide to be relatively concise, quick, and non-assuming. Hopefully it is a good video that teaches you a lot and gives you the courage needed to swap over to linux.","viewCount":109260,"lengthSeconds":1871,"watchProgress":0.172731,"timeWatched":1776300396811,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"0eYbtgBtp8jLP82S","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
