{"videoId":"NKkI-LwNOhw","title":"Customize Hyprland with Lua (2027 Edition)","author":"tony","authorId":"UC65_CVnMw6hvPET_DRDg3GA","published":1778763644000,"description":"This is a quick and painless tutorial on how to customize Hyprland using Lua, on version 0.55.0.\n \n<b>Config Files:</b> https://github.com/tonybanters/hyprlua-btw\n<b>XMPP Room</b> xmpp:tonybtw@conference.xmpp.tonybtw.com?join\n<b>Ko-Fi:</b> https://ko-fi.com/tonybtw\n\n<b>Music:</b>\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RPrgNFnbAhQ\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Jy7FMagiTFk\n\nChapters\n0:00 Intro\n1:33 NixOS Hyprland Install\n4:30 Create Hyprland v0.55.0 Flake\n7:36 Pass Hyprland Flake into Config\n9:02 Reboot and Upadate Foot Config\n10:31 Generate Lua LSP File\n12:07 Create .luarc.json File\n14:19 First Launch into Hyprland\n15:20 Update Cosmetics, Gaps, Corners\n16:38 Keyboard Input Settings\n18:03 swaybg Set Wallpaper\n20:34 Firefox Window Rule\n21:57 Update Keybinds\n25:50 Obligatory Neofetch\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/hyprland\">#hyprland</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/linux\">#linux</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/lua\">#lua</a>","viewCount":18058,"lengthSeconds":1559,"watchProgress":1279.678448,"timeWatched":1778944057600,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"yOh4X7iUqvCx98Rj","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"HleWk-vemLs","title":"How to Draw 3D Heads with Perspective","author":"Proko","authorId":"UClM2LuQ1q5WEc23462tQzBg","published":1704993875000,"description":"This is a great exercise to improve your perspective skills, especially with organic forms like human heads. You&apos;re going to figure out the orientation of the head in space by considering a simple box, then using that box as a map for a portrait. Watch this video for tips on how to do this properly. \n\nPractice this from the photos I&apos;ve provided in the link below and submit your drawing to the community on the same page!\n\nREFERENCE:\nhttps://www.proko.com/s/d6De\n\n\nCHAPTERS:\n\n00:00 - Intro\n01:11 - Level 1 Project\n03:33 - Level 2 Project\n04:43 - Outro\n\n\nRELATED LINKS:\n\nPerspective for Beginners - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BYlW8XC0MlI\nTwo-Point Perspective Drawing Made Simple - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9-Y4K4hqZwo\nHow to Learn Perspective - Draftsmen S1E26 - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7MV-bJz1dcw\n\n\n\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/perspective\">#perspective</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/drawingfundamentals\">#drawingfundamentals</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/hashtag/portraitdrawing\">#portraitdrawing</a>\n\n\nSubscribe to Proko: http://bit.ly/SubProko\nDon&apos;t miss new tutorials - Hit the BELL!\n\nPremium Videos - http://www.proko.com/store\nPose photo sets - http://www.proko.com/tools\n\n\nFOLLOW PROKO:\n\nEmail Newsletter- http://www.proko.com/subscribe\nInstagram - https://www.instagram.com/stanprokopenko/\nTwitter - https://twitter.com/StanProkopenko\nFacebook - https://www.facebook.com/prokotv\nTumblr - http://stanprokopenko.tumblr.com/\nPinterest - https://www.pinterest.com/stanprokopenko/pins/\n\n\nWATCH MORE PROKO:\n\nLatest Uploads: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-Pu1uGh1-Y4&list=PLtG4P3lq8RHH0YGMCXa4uWsHVwTDkDcpN&index=1\nFigure Drawing: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=74HR59yFZ7Y&list=PLtG4P3lq8RHGuMuprDarMz_Y9Fbw_d2ws&index=1\nArt of Caricature: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FOURPIkpPXk&list=PLtG4P3lq8RHEkeRGn6aFRct0kq4oDwwTa&index=1\nPopular Videos: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1EPNYWeEf1U&list=PLtG4P3lq8RHHR_SKsGtufNd8uo2L7_vTQ&index=1\n\n\nABOUT PROKO:\n\nInstructional How to Draw videos for artists. My drawing lessons are approachable enough for beginners and detailed enough for advanced artists. My philosophy is to teach timeless concepts in an entertaining way. I believe that when you are having fun, you learn better. I take pride in producing high-quality videos that you will enjoy watching and re-watching.\n\n\nCREDITS:\n\nArtist | Instructor - Stan Prokopenko (http://www.stanprokopenko.com/)\nProducer - Stan Prokopenko, Charlie Nicholson\nProduction Assistance - Hongju Lim, Stephen Clark (http://www.peppermintgentleman.com/), Charlie Nicholson\nEditing - Hongju Lim (https://www.hongjulim.com/), Charlie Nicholson (https://www.instagram.com/shloogorgh/)\nPublishing - Alex Otis\n\nAdditional model images from Grafit Studio () and Satine Zillah ()\n\nMusic Used with Permission Intro - The Freak Fandango Orchestra \nAdditional music by Epidemic Sound","viewCount":231875,"lengthSeconds":363,"watchProgress":0,"timeWatched":1780486556437,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"yyBfXIbbknsstPOQ","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
{"videoId":"oTOu7VfXnl8","title":"the dream music player, finally.","author":"Bread on Penguins","authorId":"UCwHwDuNd9lCdA7chyyquDXw","published":1747855821000,"description":"the dream terminal (CLI) music player. a rust mpd client with full album art support, extreme UI customization, proper resizing, and more. hoping this is the last music player I ever switch to :&apos;)\n\nrmpc: https://mierak.github.io/rmpc/\nmpd: https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Music_Player_Daemon\n\nhttps://github.com/BreadOnPenguins/dots/tree/master/.config/rmpc\nhttps://github.com/BreadOnPenguins/dots/blob/master/.config/wal/templates/pywal16.ron\n\n0:00 context\n3:09 quick walkthrough of the features\n4:42 configuration and example layouts\n\nPainting is by Alois Arnegger titled Alpine Glow.","viewCount":348361,"lengthSeconds":484,"watchProgress":0.383336,"timeWatched":1776304594741,"isLive":false,"type":"video","_id":"z0lWakafKiDVphZx","lastViewedPlaylistType":"","lastViewedPlaylistItemId":null}
